# Committed eval summaries are read as diffs, so their line endings must not
# depend on who checked them out. Git for Windows' installer defaults
# core.autocrlf to true, which would rewrite these to CRLF on checkout and
# show every line as changed on the next commit. core.autocrlf is unset on the
# machine this was added from, so the hazard is latent rather than live here.
#
# Deliberately narrow: the repo has 20+ unanchored .gitignore patterns and no
# line-ending policy anywhere else, and choosing one for the whole polyglot
# tree is not this brief's call. Only the files whose diffs are the deliverable
# are pinned.
backend/eval/results/*.md text eol=lf
